From 50fba0d1cf8fc0527443e673392bb004ff42350c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrosha <114847463+JRoshangah@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:43:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Add a table-approved take-back with a curated fix-up tool
 set

A player can ask the table to undo a misplay. Every other human has to
allow it, and the requester then gets a two-minute window with a small
set of board fix-ups. Nothing is rewound by the engine: the board is
corrected by hand, and the game log records the request and the result.

- TakeBackCoordinator keeps the request on the host - who asked, how each
  human voted, and how long the window has left. AI opponents do not vote,
  so a game against AI alone grants straight away. A vote nobody answers
  lapses after a minute.
- TakeBackTools runs the fix-ups: untap, tap, move a card to another zone,
  set a life total, add or remove counters, refill mana. All but the card
  move reuse the matching Dev Mode action, whose prompts already work for
  a network client because the host runs that client's controller.
- takeBackAction and takeBackTool travel over IGameController and the net
  protocol, and the host refuses a tool unless that player's window is
  open, so a client cannot reach the fix-ups any other way.
- VTakeBackDialog is one non-modal dialog that turns from a vote tally
  into the tool box, a watcher notice, or the outcome, with a countdown.
